From 06b6c632f87cb35c492dd0e5f69829f82761bbd7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alper Ak <alperyasinak1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 26 Dec 2025 13:23:38 +0300
Subject: tpm: tpm_i2c_infineon: Fix locality leak on get_burstcount() failure

[ Upstream commit bbd6e97c836cbeb9606d7b7e5dcf8a1d89525713 ]

get_burstcount() can return -EBUSY on timeout. When this happens, the
function returns directly without releasing the locality that was
acquired at the beginning of tpm_tis_i2c_send().

Use goto out_err to ensure proper cleanup when get_burstcount() fails.

Fixes: aad628c1d91a ("char/tpm: Add new driver for Infineon I2C TIS TPM")
Signed-off-by: Alper Ak <alperyasinak1@gmail.com>
Reviewed-by: Jarkko Sakkinen <jarkko@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Jarkko Sakkinen <jarkko@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Ulrich Hecht <uli@kernel.org>
---
 drivers/char/tpm/tpm_i2c_infineon.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/char/tpm/tpm_i2c_infineon.c b/drivers/char/tpm/tpm_i2c_infineon.c
index 3b4e9672ff6cdb..aa38b4dcfdf03a 100644
--- a/drivers/char/tpm/tpm_i2c_infineon.c
+++ b/drivers/char/tpm/tpm_i2c_infineon.c
@@ -549,8 +549,10 @@ static int tpm_tis_i2c_send(struct tpm_chip *chip, u8 *buf, size_t len)
 		burstcnt = get_burstcount(chip);
 
 		/* burstcnt < 0 = TPM is busy */
-		if (burstcnt < 0)
-			return burstcnt;
+		if (burstcnt < 0) {
+			rc = burstcnt;
+			goto out_err;
+		}
 
 		if (burstcnt > (len - 1 - count))
 			burstcnt = len - 1 - count;
-- 
